# 7. HPA vs VPA

| Feature | HPA | VPA |
|---|---|---|
| Scaling Type | Horizontal | Vertical |
| Action | Adds or removes pods | Adjusts CPU and memory |
| Main Purpose | Handle changing traffic | Optimize pod resources |
| Typical Use | Web applications | Resource-intensive workloads |
| Pod Restart | Usually not required for scaling | May be required |

**Important:** Using HPA and VPA together on the same resource metrics can cause conflicts and unstable scaling behavior.

