# 8. Goldilocks

## What is Goldilocks?

Goldilocks is an open-source Kubernetes tool developed by Fairwinds.

It provides recommendations for CPU and memory requests and limits using VPA recommendations.

It helps prevent resource requests and limits from being too high or too low.

## Install Goldilocks

Add Helm repository:

```bash
helm repo add fairwinds-stable https://charts.fairwinds.com/stable
```

Create namespace:

```bash
kubectl create namespace goldilocks
```

Install Goldilocks:

```bash
helm install goldilocks --namespace goldilocks fairwinds-stable/goldilocks
```

Enable Goldilocks for namespaces:

```bash
kubectl label ns goldilocks goldilocks.fairwinds.com/enabled=true
```

```bash
kubectl label namespace default goldilocks.fairwinds.com/enabled=true
```

Expose dashboard:

```bash
kubectl patch svc goldilocks-dashboard -n goldilocks -p '{"spec": {"type": "LoadBalancer"}}'
```

Check service:

```bash
